1
CITY OF CHEYENNE PARKS AND RECREATION DEPARTMENT
ICE AND EVENTS CENTER USER AGREEMENT

This Agreement (“Agreement”), dated this _______ day of ___________________,
2013, is by and between the City of Cheyenne, a municipal corporation organized under the laws
of the State of Wyoming (“City”), located at 2101 O’Neil Avenue, Cheyenne, Wyoming 82001,
and Cheyenne Warriors Professional Indoor Football Tean, LLC, a limited liability company
organized under the laws of the State of Wyoming (“Cheyenne Warriors”), having its principal
office at 113 West 17th Street, Cheyenne, Wyoming 82001.  This Agreement pertains to the City
of Cheyenne Owned Ice and Events Center (“Events Center”) located at 1530 West Lincolnway,
Cheyenne, Wyoming 82001.  The Events Center is administered by the City of Cheyenne Parks
and Recreation Department (“City”).

WHEREAS, the City owns, manages, and operates the Events Center and has the power
and authority to lease the use thereof to others for the purpose of conducting certain events and
other activities; and

WHEREAS, Cheyenne Warriors desires to use certain portions of the Events Center as
indicated on Appendix A to this Agreement and the City desires to license the use thereof to
Cheyenne Warriors, for the purpose of holding and presenting arena football games and related
practices (collectively referred to herein as the “Event”), all subject to the terms and conditions
set forth in this Agreement.

NOW, THEREFORE, in consideration of the covenants and agreements contained
herein, and intending to be legally bound hereby, the parties agree as follows:

1.
Premises.  City hereby grants to Cheyenne Warriors permission to use those portions of
the Center set forth on Appendix A, attached hereto and incorporated herein (the "Premises"),
upon the terms and conditions contained herein.  Only Cheyenne Warriors' members, prospective
members, designated representatives and invitees are permitted by this agreement to use the
Premises.

2.
Term.  The period of Cheyenne Warriors’ use of the Premises shall be from March 28,
2013 through July 30, 2013 (the “Term”).  Before the commencement of the term of this
Agreement as set forth in Appendix A, the City shall make the Center available to Cheyenne
Warriors, upon the payment of separate and additional charges, for (i) preparation of the Event
and delivery, move-in and set-up of Cheyenne Warriors’ property and equipment; and (ii) load-
out immediately following the conclusion of the Event, ending no later than the time set forth on
Appendix A.  Unless otherwise expressly stated herein, or otherwise agreed to in writing, all
deliveries and items required for presentation of the Event shall be provided at the sole cost and
expense of Cheyenne Warriors.

3.
Purpose.  Cheyenne Warriors shall be permitted to use the Premises solely for the
purpose set forth in Appendix A.  Cheyenne Warriors is not permitted to use the Premises for
other purposes.
```

### Page 2 of 12

```text
2

4.
Fees.

A.
In consideration for City permission to use the Premises, Cheyenne Warriors shall
pay user fees to the City according to the following rate schedule:

i.
Games - $150.00 per hour starting at 4:00pm and ending at 11:00pm in
addition to the $150.00 daily fee for a total of $1200.00.

ii.
$150.00 for each day that turf is laid out on the arena floor.

B.
The user fee for a Game shall be paid for on or before the Monday prior to the
Game.

C.
The daily user fee for turf shall be paid in advance and shall be paid in a lump
sum on or before the last day of the month prior to any month in which turf is to be paid out on
the arena floor.  For example, the daily user fee for April shall be computed by multiplying the
number of days that turf will be laid out of the arena floor by the daily fee specified in subsection
A., and all such fees shall be paid in a lump sum on or before March 31.

D.
All user fees owed to the City shall be paid with Credit Card/Cashiers
Check/Money Order or Cash.  The City will not accept checks as payment for user fees.

F.
In the event Cheyenne Warriors fails, neglects, or refuses to pay the user fees at
the times and in the amounts specified herein, the City may, in addition to other remedies
provided by law, declare a forfeiture of this Agreement and may revoke the permission granted
herein to Cheyenne Warriors to use the Premises for the purposes stated herein until such time as
Cheyenne Warriors complies with the terms and conditions of this Agreement.

E.
In addition to the payment of user fees as stated above, Cheyenne Warriors agrees
to provide no less than five (5) workers to assist with the installation of turf and with the removal
of turf to accommodate special events which may be scheduled in the Events Center by the City
so long as such events are not scheduled during game times or related practice times.  This
service will be provided by Cheyenne Warriors at no charge to the City.

5.
Liquor.  Prior to the sale, possession or consumption of alcoholic liquors or malt
beverages at the Events Center, Cheyenne Warriors shall comply with all state laws and with
applicable City ordinances, regulations and policies, including permit requirements  pursuant to
Chapter 5.12 of the Cheyenne City Code.  The Chief of Police may require Cheyenne Warriors
to provide on-site security, through law enforcement personnel, during any Event which involves
the sale, possession or consumption of alcoholic liquors or malt beverages.  The City reserves the
right to deny applications for permits under Chapter 5.12 of the Cheyenne City Code in the event
of repeated or consistent violations of state or local liquor laws or the terms and conditions of
this Agreement.
```

