6.
Advertising.  The City will allow Cheyenne Warriors to display advertising in the interior
portions of the Events Center as stated in Appendix B (see attached form).

7.
Property–Liability.  With the express prior written approval of the City’s Recreation
Coordinator–Ice and Events, Cheyenne Warriors shall be permitted to install items of personal
property within the team locker rooms which may be used by Cheyenne Warriors in connection
with arena football games and practices, provided however, that the installation of any such
items shall not be permitted if installation would result in any significant damage or injury to the
Events Center or to any equipment, facilities, or components thereof.  Any such items installed
by Cheyenne Warriors shall be removed from the Events Center within a reasonable period of
time following the termination of this Agreement.  Cheyenne Warriors shall be liable for the cost
of repair or replacement of any and all City property which is damaged or destroyed as a result of
Cheyenne Warriors’ use of the Events Center, normal wear and tear excepted.  Cheyenne
Warriors expressly assumes liability for any loss or damage to City property which is caused by
its principals, officers, employees, agents, representatives, volunteers or players.  Cheyenne
Warriors expressly assumes liability for any loss or damage to City property caused by persons
or entities who have been invited by Cheyenne Warriors to be present at the Events Center for
purposes permitted under this Agreement, and for any such loss or damage caused by their
officers, employees, agents, representatives, volunteers or players.  In addition, any person who
causes any loss, injury or damage to the Events Center or to any other property or facilities of the
City may be banned from the Events Center by the Recreation Coordinator–Ice and Events, in
his or her sole discretion, after consultation with Cheyenne Warriors.

8.
Failure to Pay.  In the event that Cheyenne Warriors fails to pay user fees required by this
Agreement on or before the specific payment dates, the City reserves the right to impose finance
charges equal to 1.5 % per month (18% per annum) on such unpaid amounts.  In the event of
default of payment pursuant to Section 21 below, the City reserves the right to terminate this
Agreement and retain all fees previously paid by Cheyenne Warriors.  Costs of collection and
reasonable attorney’s fees incurred in connection therewith shall be paid by Cheyenne Warriors.

9.
City’s Responsibilities.  The City will provide the following during Cheyenne Warriors’
periods of use of the Premises.

A.
Electricity and other utilities for lighting, heating and air conditioning, as
customarily provided by the City for similar events at the Events Center.

B.
Cleaning and janitorial services will be provided by City staff in locker rooms 3
and 4 only when a representative of Cheyenne Warriors is present.  Cheyenne Warriors shall be
generally responsible for janitorial maintenance in locker rooms 3 and 4.

C.
City staff customarily provided for similar events at the Events Center.
