business days after receipt.

10.
Cheyenne Warriors’ Responsibilities. Cheyenne Warriors agrees to comply with the
following terms and conditions during its use of the Premises.

A.
Except as otherwise permitted by the City, no alcoholic beverages, malt beverages
or glass containers shall be brought on the Premises, by players, coaches or staff.

 B.
No outside food or beverages may be consumed by players, coaches, officers,
directors or business invitees of Cheyenne Warriors in the absence of express written consent of
the City’s Director of Leisure Services or the Recreation Coordinator–Ice and Events, provided,
however, that Cheyenne Warriors’ sponsors may choose to donate meals to be consumed by
Cheyenne Warriors players, coaches, and team officials on game days if such donations are
approved by the Recreation Coordinator Ice and Events.  Requests for approval of donations
must be submitted to the Recreation Coordinator at least two weeks (14 days) prior to donation.

C.
Since Cheyenne Warriors’ use of the Premises is for the purpose of playing arena
football, all players shall wear a helmet and necessary protective equipment as required by the
City or applicable rules developed by organizations which govern the sport of arena football.

D.
Cheyenne Warriors shall strictly adhere to the dates and the starting and finishing
times of its permitted periods of use as set forth in Appendix A.

E.
Cheyenne Warriors shall comply with all rules and regulations of the Events
Center and with the directions of City personnel responsible for the operation or security of the
Events Center.

F.
Cheyenne Warriors shall provide security personnel if requested by the City
pursuant to Sections 5 and 14 of this Agreement.
