5

G.
Cheyenne Warriors agrees not to do any act or allow any act to be done during the
Term of this Agreement which shall mar, deface or injure any part of the Events Center.  Upon
expiration of the Term, Cheyenne Warriors shall surrender possession of the Premises to the City
in as good condition and repair as at the beginning of the Term, excepting normal wear and tear.

H.
Cheyenne Warriors shall use the Events Center and Premises only in a safe and
careful manner.

I.
Cheyenne Warriors shall notify the City in writing of the cancellation of any
practice or game at least seventy-two (72) hours prior to the date of the practice or game.  In the
event, Cheyenne Warriors fails to provide at least seventy-two (72) hours notice of the
cancellation of any game or practice, Cheyenne Warriors will remain liable for the user fee for
the practice or game time.  In the event the Events Center is closed by the City due to inclement
weather, road closures, or other unusual events, the City may, in its discretion, refund user fees
which were paid in advance subject to such terms and conditions as may be imposed by the City.
The City retains the right, in its sole discretion, to close the Events Center after consultation with
Cheyenne Warriors.

J.
The birthday party room located in the lobby is available for Cheyenne Warriors’
use with a charge of $25.00 per hour and at the discretion of the City.  All use by the Cheyenne
Warriors of the aforementioned room must be scheduled prior to its use through the City’s
Recreation Coordinator–Ice and Events.  Any scheduled use will be charged the hourly rate.

K.
During games, Cheyenne Warriors does not have exclusive use of the entire
facility.  Thus, other areas of the Events Center, such as the lobby, arcade, laser tag room, and
birthday party room will remain open for regular public use.  Cheyenne Warriors may rent the
entire Events Center facility at regular rental rates if exclusive use of the entire facility is desired.
For game use, the Cheyenne Warriors will have exclusive use of inner arena areas including
arena football surface, spectator stands, and team locker rooms.

L.
All items of personal property owned by Cheyenne Warriors which may be stored
in the team locker rooms or anywhere else on the premises shall be removed prior to the end of
the Term of this Agreement.  Cheyenne Warriors, and its officers, directors, members,
employees, agents, representatives, players, guests, invitees, and volunteers, shall be responsible
for the reasonable and necessary cost of repairing or replacing any items within the team locker
rooms which are damaged or destroyed as a result of Cheyenne Warriors’ activities under this
Agreement.  The City shall not be responsible for lost or stolen articles.

M.
Cheyenne Warriors will pay the following charges for use of the City’s
photocopier: $0.20 per black and white copy and $0.30 per color copy.  Cheyenne Warriors will
be invoiced on a monthly basis.

N.
Cheyenne Warriors may sell approved merchandise in designated areas only.
Cheyenne Warriors will retain 100% of merchandise sales.   The placement of merchandise and
the sale thereof must be approved by the City Clerk and Cheyenne Warriors must obtain any and
all permits which may be required for merchandise sales.
