### Page 8 of 12

```text
8

A.
If requested by the City, Cheyenne Warriors shall provide and pay for its own
security personnel in sufficient numbers to police Cheyenne Warriors’ use of the Premises and
any spectators, guests or invitees attending any Cheyenne Warriors’ event.  Any security
personnel to be provided by Cheyenne Warriors must be approved in writing by the City’s Chief
of Police, or authorized designee, no later than ten (10) days in advance of Cheyenne Warriors’
use of the Premises.  In the event the City requests Cheyenne Warriors to provide such security
and Cheyenne Warriors fails to obtain City approval of personnel in a timely fashion or fails to
provide adequate security, as determined by the City in its sole discretion, the City shall have the
right to provide security personnel at the regular rate for weekday duty and at double-time rate
for weekend duty to be paid by Cheyenne Warriors or, alternatively, shall have the right to
terminate this Agreement.

B.
If, in the sole judgment of the City, Cheyenne Warriors’ use of the Premises at
any time creates an unreasonable risk of harm to the safety of the Events Center, City property,
or persons on the Premises, the City reserves the right to eject from the Premises any person
making use of the Premises through or in association with Cheyenne Warriors, to restrict
Cheyenne Warriors’ activities on the Premises, to cancel any period of Cheyenne Warriors’ use
of the Premises or to terminate this Agreement in its entirety.  Any such action by the City shall
not be deemed to be a breach of this Agreement and the City shall not be liable for damages for
such an action, nor shall the City be obligated to return to Cheyenne Warriors any portion of any
fee paid to City hereunder.  The City’s reservation of rights in this section shall not in any way
relieve or limit Cheyenne Warriors’ duty to indemnify the City pursuant to this Agreement.

15.
Responsibility for Safety.  City and Cheyenne Warriors’ personnel shall inspect the
Premises prior to each use thereof by Cheyenne Warriors.  It is mutually understood and agreed
that Cheyenne Warriors’ use of the Premises and the Events Center may be suspended by the
City in its sole discretion if an inspection reveals hazards or defects which present an
unreasonable risk of harm.

16.
Assumption of Risk.  Cheyenne Warriors, and all persons using the Events Center and
Premises hereunder, for any purpose, under this Agreement, and all invitees of Cheyenne
Warriors, assume all risk and danger incidental to the use of the Events Center and Premises for
the purposes of this Agreement.  Since Cheyenne Warriors is using the Premises for the purpose
of conducting arena football games and practices, Cheyenne Warriors acknowledges that there
are inherent risks and dangers including, without limitation, the danger of being injured,
paralyzed, or killed through contact with other players or objects in connection with arena
football.

17.
Control of Premises.  The City and its authorized representatives shall have the right at all
times to enter upon and have access to the Events Center and the Premises.  In contracting the
use of the Premises to Cheyenne Warriors, it is understood that the City does not relinquish the
right to control the management thereof and to enforce all necessary rules and regulations.  The
decision of City’s representative as to the number of persons that can safely and freely move
about in the Events Center shall be final.
