### Page 9 of 12

```text
9
18.
Reservation of Rights. The City reserves all rights not expressly granted to Cheyenne
Warriors hereunder, and may, during the Term, use any or all portions of the Premises not
specifically licensed to Cheyenne Warriors hereunder.  The City reserves the right to eject from
the Events Center and Premises any person for any reason which the City, in its sole discretion,
deems sufficient, after consultation with Cheyenne Warriors.

19.
Licenses.  The City shall secure licenses and permits that may be required by or in
connection with use of the Premises for the Event which may be required by any performing arts
societies, such as ASCAP, BMI and/or SESAC.

20.
Promotional Activity.  Cheyenne Warriors agrees not to publicly conduct any
promotional activity and not to advertise any Event to be conducted at the Events Center without
the prior consent of the City.  In addition to the requirement that promotional and advertising
must have the prior approval of the City, all advertising and promotional activities relating to the
Event shall be the sole responsibility of Cheyenne Warriors.

21.
Termination.  In the event Cheyenne Warriors at any time fails to comply with any of the
terms and conditions of this Agreement, and fails to cure such non-compliance within five (5)
days of its receipt of written notice from the City describing such noncompliance, the City may
terminate this Agreement and retain as damages any fees paid by Cheyenne Warriors under this
Agreement, without prejudice to any other legal rights or remedies the City may have.

22.
Assignment.  Cheyenne Warriors may not assign its right to use the Premises to any other
person, group or organization without the express written consent of the City which the City may
grant or withhold, in its sole discretion.

23.
Independent Contractors.  The relationship between the City and Cheyenne Warriors is
that of independent contractors and not agents or employees.  Under no circumstances shall this
Agreement be considered a contract of partnership or joint venture.  Neither party shall be liable
for any of the debts, accounts, obligations or other liabilities of the other party, and neither party
shall have any authority to obligate or bind the other party in any manner except as may be
expressly provided herein.

24.
Force Majeure.  In the event the City is unable to perform any of the terms or conditions
of this Agreement due to events or causes outside the City’s control, such as destruction or
damage to the Events Center or Premises or the unfitness of the Events Center or Premises for
occupancy as a result of fire or act of God, riot, labor, strike, national or local emergency, or
other cause not entirely within its control, the City shall not be deemed to be in breach of this
Agreement or liable to Cheyenne Warriors for damages, but shall return to Cheyenne Warriors
any portion of the fees paid to the City by Cheyenne Warriors, less the cost of any expenses
incurred by the City hereunder.

25.
Applicable Law.  This Agreement shall be construed and enforced in accordance with the
laws of the State of Wyoming.  Any disputes arising from this Agreement shall be brought in the
courts of the First Judicial District, Laramie County, Wyoming.
